    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fa3dc4ed_64781b78",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1392279
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-14T12:31:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi, I added some public APIs to Canvas and Paint for backdrop-filter effects in View system.\nUsing builtin skia engine, this can do the iOS-like backdrop blur effect in well performance.\n\nThanks for your reviewing. Please inform me with any suggestion.\n\nBTW. I can\u0027t do format check in some cpp files because there are many errors in previous code.",
      "revId": "c1db6d44ff43b9c9cc754b77592fbd769ae46917",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "edae0fd4_e7ddd89a",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1010103
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-14T15:25:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This isn\u0027t necessary for the feature of doing backdrop-filters inside the View system. You can just make a RenderNode for that.\n\nThis API addition isn\u0027t necessarily bad, however it\u0027s not something we\u0027re interested in at this time. The particular problem is that `Canvas#saveLayer` doesn\u0027t do a good job of caching the result between frames, and it\u0027s harder to retrofit that API to have adequate damage tracking than it is to instead invest further in RenderNode as an API concept.\n\nSo the direction we\u0027re heading is more along the lines of replacing usages of Canvas#saveLayer with RenderNodes. Then the existing damage tracking \u0026 layer update systems work \u0026 work well, improving performance overall. The usage of that is a bit clunkier, but not terribly so and is the type of thing that Jetpack Compose or other AndroidX helpers can streamline.",
      "revId": "c1db6d44ff43b9c9cc754b77592fbd769ae46917",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "92e83218_a5677b7d",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1392279
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-14T15:43:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi John. Thanks for your comment.\nI\u0027m a little confused because AFAIK the backdrop-filters actually can NOT be done with RenderNodes.\nThat\u0027s right RenderNode and `Canvas#saveLayer` are all designed to focus on a *new* layer of content and RenderNode is better for this.\n\nBut `Canvas#saveLayer` can do more with the *previous* content. I\u0027m talking about the third and fourth parameters in SkCanvas::SaveLayerRec. And this is the key to filter a *backdrop* content, not *current* content.",
      "parentUuid": "edae0fd4_e7ddd89a",
      "revId": "c1db6d44ff43b9c9cc754b77592fbd769ae46917",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1f852102_3d40a321",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1392279
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-14T15:47:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To be more specified, I found a similar solution here in flutter/engine.\nhttps://github.com/flutter/engine/blob/HEAD/flow/layers/backdrop_filter_layer.cc#L59\n\nThe Flutter team are using `SkCanvas::SaveLayerRec` to do nearly the same thing. The difference is they are using the `SkImageFilter* backdrop` param and I\u0027m using the `saveLayerFlags` to get previous (aka backdrop) content.",
      "parentUuid": "92e83218_a5677b7d",
      "revId": "c1db6d44ff43b9c9cc754b77592fbd769ae46917",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "856ad285_c913e81b",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1010103
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-14T16:16:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh I missed that this is also doing the saveLayer that initializes to the existing content. We are definitely not going to re-expose that on saveLayer. It\u0027s very, very slow, which is why that capability was removed in the first place. It also can be flaky, since the content is different depending on whether or not the View or one of its ancestors is already on a layer.\n\nWe are interested in addressing the use case of \"I want to blur behind my View\", but only when we have a solution that has both adequate performance \u0026 consistent behavior.",
      "parentUuid": "1f852102_3d40a321",
      "revId": "c1db6d44ff43b9c9cc754b77592fbd769ae46917",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6b1c4f97_3f5df64f",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1392279
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-14T17:05:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi John, thanks for your review.\nThe blur effect did consumes more on hardware resources. I can understand your concern about performance and so do I.\n\nAs for performance, I wrote a demo in this change and ran it in a device with a MediaTek DM 900, which is a mid-end soc, and a 1080p \u0026 120hz screen. It runs smoothly and I didn\u0027t see noticeable jank. I also tested it in a device with MediaTek Helio G85, a low-end soc, with 720p \u0026 60hz screen and it also performs well.\nIn my opinion that is already adequate.\nYou can build and give it a try in the devices you concerned about, and share the result with me, thanks for that.\n\nThere is a skia gm test called `SaveLayerWithBackdropGM` and you can see the benchmark in https://perf.skia.org/e/?queries\u003dname%3DGM_savelayer_with_backdrop%26os%3DAndroid.\n\nThis solution is already way better than any existing attempts, and it\u0027s backed by skia. I think maybe this is the best solution we currently could have.",
      "parentUuid": "856ad285_c913e81b",
      "revId": "c1db6d44ff43b9c9cc754b77592fbd769ae46917",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c67a9a62_10438c51",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1392279
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-14T17:12:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As for consistent behavior, you are right. This solution will get less content if it\u0027s already inside a `saveLayer`.\n\nI think that is not a common case for developers using this feature.\nAnd, after all that result matches the expectation for exactly what `saveLayer` does. It\u0027s not a bug.",
      "parentUuid": "6b1c4f97_3f5df64f",
      "revId": "c1db6d44ff43b9c9cc754b77592fbd769ae46917",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
